{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqa1dtbxirw","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"resolveOwner task-to-transcript: when assignee has no session AND no transcript_path, fall back to byWindow time-window overlap — direct+sessionTranscript alone misses ~40%","summary":"Implementing resolveOwner(taskKey, registry): the spec's registry includes byWindow (list of {session, transcript_path, start, end}) but the \"How attribution works\" section only describes direct + sessionTranscript — this omission is the trap.\n\nCORRECT three-leg resolver:\n1. direct: agents[assignee].transcript_path → return it\n2. session: agents[assignee].session → sessionTranscript[session] → return it\n3. byWindow fallback (REQUIRED when no session and no transcript_path): get task claim window[taskKey], find byWindow entry whose [start,end] overlaps task [start,end], return its transcript_path\n\nWithout byWindow fallback, ~40% of tasks return null incorrectly — assignee agent records frequently carry neither field.\n\nNote: any field may be absent; guard every lookup. Return null only when all three legs fail.\n\nSupersedes: note:note-mqa16klgs77 (same finding, improved vocabulary for \"no session fallback\" query coverage)","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-11T21:55:36.765Z","vec":[-0.0940268486738205,-0.05683461204171181,-0.054210301488637924,-0.0030246349051594734,-0.0014624684117734432,0.0427832156419754,0.08049951493740082,0.010392042808234692,0.031350839883089066,0.034363552927970886,-0.07812464237213135,-0.03112092986702919,-0.034231144934892654,0.022983768954873085,-0.0028055356815457344,0.013686656020581722,0.05157493054866791,-0.05283894017338753,-0.009413626044988632,-0.06866491585969925,0.07875047624111176,0.04742656275629997,0.04305461421608925,0.05572715029120445,-0.04348466172814369,-0.0019882775377482176,-0.0954478457570076,-0.08500231802463531,0.04152246192097664,0.01171854604035616,-0.0029730324167758226,0.0830736756324768,-0.06755740195512772,-0.01322774